weaknesses.value:
1. The organization can be further improved (the organization of Methodology does not follow Fig. 1), which makes the paper sometimes hard to follow (probably due to the complexity introduced by assembling 3 stages for tackling the problem);

2. The novelty of this paper would be a major concern. It seems the proposed algorithm in this paper simply assembles three stages, each with an existing method. The orientation regressor is from [9]. The feature extractor is the modified DGCNN proposed in [22]. The non-rigid registration mainly follows [18].

3. The submission and main paper have different titles. Please fix it.

questions.value:
1. Why is the proposed method unsupervised? It seems the orientation regressor requires the ground-truth pose to the canonical space. And the PointInFoNCE loss (Eq. 4) also requires correspondence labels? Or the authors call the generalization from one dataset to the other datasets the unsupervised learning?

2. How good is the orientation regressor? Can it deal with large translations? e.g., the translation introduced by a walking human. From my experiences, this kind of pose regressor can only overfit to a specific model and hard to generalize. Also, it is usually not very accurate (correct me if I was wrong);

3. Why all the models are called "pre-trained"? Should it be generalizing a model trained on the same task to new data?

